💡 **SUGGESTION: Redundant map entry — `.crap-baseline.json` is already covered by the dot-file filter**

```js
const NON_AGENT_ROOT_JSON = {
    'versions.json': true,
    '.crap-baseline.json': true   // ← redundant
};
...
.filter((f) => f.endsWith('.json') && !NON_AGENT_ROOT_JSON[f] && !f.startsWith('.'))
```

The same filter's `!f.startsWith('.')` already excludes `.crap-baseline.json` (and every other dot-file), so the map entry is dead weight that suggests it does something extra. Keeping only `'versions.json'` in the map (the one real exception) makes the two mechanisms read cleanly: map = named non-agents, prefix = dot-files. Purely cosmetic — behavior is identical.

